in nethack2.3e (unix) when you're full it says so at the bottom of the screen
(i.e. Satiated). so if you eat when you're already full you should run the risk
of choking on your food. however since walking into a pool of water isn't
always fatal then perhaps overeating shouldn't always be fatal. perhaps a
good vomit until you're weak is in order. other possibilities have been
mentioned which seem okay also. back to the water ... if you stumble in and
teleport out (thank goodness) you should pay some price, perhaps rusted weapon
a/o armor, dissolved scrolls, watered-down wasteless potions, water-logged
wands and the like, of course, you shouldn't be thirsty afterwards ... and
the thirst idea mentioned before seems appropriate also. certainly drowning
and fatally overeating are bad luck but getting rescued from either could
conceivably cost you luck points also ...

